Subject: [PATCH] avutil/vulkan: preserve derived DRM context and consumer fences

The DRM exporter must retain a caller-provided derived frames context. Replacing
it with the Vulkan source context leaks the caller reference and prevents the
public map API from recognizing an unmap, causing an unnecessary re-import and
an observed roundtrip stall. Keep the existing fallback for internal callers
which provide no destination context.

Importing after a DRM consumer may write the frame again. Export implicit
readers as well as writers when WRITE mapping is requested; READ-only mapping
continues to wait only for writers. Linux dma-buf defines WRITE/RW export as
waiting for all usage. Retain semaphore, ownership and cleanup behavior.

Base: FFmpeg n9.0.2/946fcce with the separate actual-image-usage patch.
Reviewed master fa4daf630e retains the context overwrite and READ-only flag.
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, matching the modified upstream file.

--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
@@ -3574,7 +3574,7 @@
             };
             VkImportSemaphoreFdInfoKHR import_info;
             struct dma_buf_export_sync_file implicit_fd_info = {
-                .flags = DMA_BUF_SYNC_READ,
+                .flags = flags & AV_HWFRAME_MAP_WRITE ? DMA_BUF_SYNC_RW : DMA_BUF_SYNC_READ,
                 .fd = -1,
             };
 
@@ -4349,7 +4349,8 @@
     dst->width   = src->width;
     dst->height  = src->height;
     dst->data[0] = (uint8_t *)drm_desc;
-    dst->hw_frames_ctx = av_buffer_ref(src->hw_frames_ctx);
+    if (!dst->hw_frames_ctx)
+        dst->hw_frames_ctx = av_buffer_ref(src->hw_frames_ctx);
 
     if (sync_fd >= 0)
         close(sync_fd);
